  "preamble": "In Australian English the word-final schwa of comma and letter words is often lowered to [ɐ], so that it closely resembles the STRUT vowel /ɐ/ (Cox & Fletcher 2017): comma [ˈkɔmɐ], letter [ˈleɾɐ]. The lowering is not categorical, and the lowered vowel remains part of the /ə/ phoneme.",
